What this FPAC node offers
--------------------------
FPAC is a ROSE network node. ROSE carries your connection from node
to node across the network, the way a telephone exchange does.

Find a station by its callsign
  Wp VK7HDM      shows the node where the station lives, its ROSE
                 address and when it was last seen.

Connect to a station by its callsign alone
  C VK7HDM-4     the node finds the address in the White Pages and
                 routes the call for you: no address, no path to type.
                 This one reaches Danny's node in Hobart, Tasmania.

Connect to a ROSE address
  C F6BVP-8 2080175520
                 a ROSE address works like a phone number: a 4-digit
                 DNIC for the country (2080 France, 5050 Australia,
                 3100 USA), then a 6-digit node number.
  DNic           lists the countries and their DNIC.

When you leave a remote node, you come back to this one.

More commands
  QSl            a QSL card confirming your connection, also as a
                 picture to download
  Routes         the ROSE routes known by this node
  Nodes          the ROSE nodes; NEtrom, the NetRom nodes
  BBs            the BBS of this node
  Help <cmd>     help on a command; ? for the list of commands
